    "summary": "Restricts any field on any model to the groups you name, as hidden or read only, enforced by the server and not only in the form view: field level security for any model: hide or lock any field for the groups you choose, enforced by the server and not just hidden in the form view",
    "tagline": "Hide a field, or lock it so nobody can change it, for everyone outside the groups you name. Set up from a screen instead of Python, and enforced by the server, not only in the form",
    "intro": [
      "Field Access Rules is for the person who is asked \"can the sales team stop seeing that field?\" on an Odoo 19 database, and who knows that deleting a field from a form view settles nothing. You pick a model, tick the fields, name the groups that keep access and choose what everyone else gets: the field is hidden, or it is read only. The rule is fed into the check Odoo itself uses before any field is read or written, so the restriction holds in exports, in searches and over the API as well. This page walks through every step with screenshots of an Odoo 19 database seeded with made-up data, and says plainly where the limits are.",
      "Install it and a Field Access Rules entry appears under Settings, for administrators only. It depends on Odoo's base module and nothing else. The screenshots were taken in an Odoo 19 Community database with the Contacts app installed for the examples: a fictitious office-supply company with one finance user, one dispatch user and one salesperson. The data is synthetic, and every name and number quoted beside a screenshot is read off that screenshot or off the test it came from."
    ],
