          "The form is one screen in two columns. On the left, the Model and the Fields the rule covers, shown as tags. On the right, Access as two radio buttons, the Groups that keep access as tags, and a Why line for whoever reads the rule in a year. Under them sits one sentence of reminder: everyone outside those groups loses the access in every view, export and API call, not only in the form.",
          "The rule gets a name by itself, built from its access, its first three fields and the model, for example Hidden: partner_latitude, partner_longitude, barcode on res.partner ; a fourth field adds three dots. The list shows every rule with its model, fields, access, groups and reason, and can be filtered by Hidden, Read only or Archived and grouped by model or by access.",
