    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does working out the change alter any user?",
        "a": "No. It writes only to the change record: the two counts, the plan text and the Planned state. Users are written only when you press Apply and confirm."
      },
      {
        "q": "What if one of my users is already in the company?",
        "a": "They are counted under Already correct and left out of the plan lines. A grant that finds everyone already in says Nothing would change."
      },
      {
        "q": "Will it break half-way through a batch?",
        "a": "The checks that Odoo itself would trip on, a default company outside the allowed list and a user with no company, are made before the first user is written, and either refuse the change or are handled as described above. The refusals come from the app, in its own words."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it change anybody's groups?",
        "a": "Only the Multi Company group, and only because Odoo does that itself when a user crosses between one company and several. The plan names the users beforehand. This app writes company access, nothing else."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happens to records already created in a company I revoke?",
        "a": "Nothing. They stay where they are. The user simply can no longer reach that company's data from now on."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I undo an applied change?",
        "a": "Not with a button. Make a new change with the opposite operation, work it out, read the plan and apply it. The old record stays as the account of what happened."
      }
    ],
