    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does it change my invoices or my accounting?",
        "a": "It adds a Commission Agents field to customers, orders and invoices, and a Commission button on invoices. It never changes an invoice's amounts. It creates vendor bills only when you press Create Bills, and they are drafts."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I pay on invoicing for some people and on payment for others?",
        "a": "Yes. The trigger belongs to the plan, and each person is on one plan per company. Staff on an Invoice posted plan and agents on an Invoice paid plan is the usual split."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happens when I change a plan?",
        "a": "Unsettled commission keeps the rate it was created with until the invoice is posted again or you run Recompute Commission on it, which rebuilds it from the plans as they are now. Settled commission is never rewritten."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it work with several companies or currencies?",
        "a": "Plans, rules, lines and settlements each belong to one company, and a user sees only their own companies'. The base is the invoice line's untaxed amount converted to the company currency, and bills are created in the company currency."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I delete an invoice I have paid commission on?",
        "a": "No. An invoice with settled commission cannot be deleted, because deleting it would erase what was paid. Reset it to draft or cancel it instead and the clawback follows."
      }
    ],
