    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does it archive the user or reassign anything?",
        "a": "No. It only reports. Reassigning is a decision about who should inherit each job, lead or activity, and the app does not guess."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does an archived user's scheduled action really keep running?",
        "a": "Yes. Archiving blocks the login and nothing else; the account keeps every group, so the job keeps its rights. The module's test suite pins this down with a control: the same user, the same action, before and after archiving."
      },
      {
        "q": "Will it find fields from my other apps?",
        "a": "Yes. It reads the model registry for every stored field that points at a user, so apps and custom modules installed on your database are covered without a list to maintain."
      },
      {
        "q": "Why are created-by and written-by not counted?",
        "a": "They point at whoever typed something once. Counting them would put every record the person ever touched into the report and bury the few you need to act on."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I check somebody who is already archived?",
        "a": "Yes. A check can be made for an archived user, and it reads their records, archived ones included."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it find tasks assigned to several people?",
        "a": "No. It counts fields that hold a single user. A field that holds a list of users, such as the assignees of a task, is not found."
      },
      {
        "q": "Who can use it?",
        "a": "Administrators only. The menu and both models are restricted to the Settings group."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can it slow my server down?",
        "a": "It runs only when you press Check, for one person, with one count query per user field. On the test database it finished in about a hundredth of a second; on a large database the cost grows with the number of records that name the person, and it writes only its own report."
      }
    ],
