          "Product is found by internal reference, then barcode, then exact name, in that order, with capitals mattering. A customer is found by full name or email, in any case. A payment method is found by name among those of the point of sale. A workbook is read from its first sheet only, with the header on the first non-blank row. A CSV file may use commas, semicolons or tabs; a semicolon file reads a comma as the decimal mark. Dates may be real Excel dates or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM; a date without a time means 12:00, in your own time zone.",
          "A decimal comma in a comma-separated file (\"4,00\") is refused. A comma counts as a thousands separator only in groups of three, as in 1,200.00. Quantities are kept to Odoo's two decimals.",
