    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What does SPC Cpk Analytics do?",
        "a": "It adds sample size, mean, standard deviation, Cp and Cpk, an individuals chart, a moving range chart and a capability histogram to a Quality Control Point, computed from the checks already recorded on it."
      },
      {
        "q": "What do I need to set up?",
        "a": "Tick Enable SPC/Cpk Analysis on a control point that has Measure-type checks with measurements and both Tolerance Min and Tolerance Max filled in."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which measurements are used?",
        "a": "Checks of the Measure type that are not still To Do. A Failed check counts and a reading of exactly 0 counts as 0. All checks of the point are used, with no date or product filter."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happens if I fill in only one tolerance limit?",
        "a": "An empty limit is read as 0. With only the upper limit typed, Cp became meaningless (29.08 in the test); with only the lower limit typed, Cp and Cpk read 0.00. There is no one-sided index."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are Cp and Cpk short-term or overall?",
        "a": "Overall: they use the sample standard deviation of every measurement on the point, which many references call Pp and Ppk. The control limits use the moving range."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it flag every out-of-control signal?",
        "a": "No. It marks points beyond a control limit (amber) and points outside the spec (red). Runs on one side of the centre line and trends are not flagged."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happens to my data if I uninstall it?",
        "a": "Every control point and check stays as it was. The app removes its one checkbox column and its form view."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it work with Odoo Community, Enterprise, Odoo.sh or Odoo Online?",
        "a": "It needs Odoo's Quality app, which is Enterprise. Third-party apps cannot be installed on Odoo Online. The tests ran on Odoo 19 Community with a stand-in for Quality; Odoo's real Quality app and Odoo.sh are not verified."
      }
    ],
