      {
        "q": "Does the map load for every visitor?",
        "a": "No. Nothing about the map loads until the visitor agrees: accepting optional cookies in Odoo's cookie bar, accepting the Functional category in Mithahara's Cookie Consent Banner, or clicking Show map when neither is installed. Signed-in employees never get it."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it send my customers' location anywhere?",
        "a": "No. Find the nearest store sorts the cards in the browser, and the page made 0 network requests after the click."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does Odoo send store addresses to a geocoder by itself?",
        "a": "On Odoo 19 (the build tested) no: editing an address clears the pin and Geolocate does the sending. On Odoo 20, yes: Odoo's own scheduled action sends a contact's edited address without a click. This page is for Odoo 19."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can a visitor search by their own postcode and see the nearest store?",
        "a": "Not from a typed postcode. Search matches text in the name and address, and nearest store uses the browser's position."
      },
      {
        "q": "How many stores can it list?",
        "a": "All published stores are in one page, with no paging. 1,013 stores made a 1.5 MB page that was ready in 0.65 s in a headless browser. More was not tested."
      },
      {
        "q": "Who can add stores?",
        "a": "Users with Contact Creation rights, because the Store fields are on contacts. Website editors manage the tags and website designers the tile URL."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is removed if I uninstall it?",
        "a": "The Store, Opening hours and Store tags fields, the tags, the three settings and the menu entries. Contacts stay and /stores answers 404."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can it show whether a store is open now?",
        "a": "No. Opening hours are text shown as typed."
      }
