    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Does it change my existing payments?",
        "a": "No payment is edited. The app adds a Fee Amount, a Fee Account and a Fee Move field to payments and a Restricted To list to journals; a payment with no fee amount behaves as before and books no entry."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the fee a real accounting entry?",
        "a": "Yes. It is a posted journal entry in the payment's journal, dated like the payment, with the reference \"Processing fee for\" and the payment's number."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it work with my chart of accounts?",
        "a": "It was tested with Odoo's generic chart of accounts and, in the unit tests, with no chart at all. A local chart was not tested."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I rely on the restriction to stop posting?",
        "a": "No. It hides the journal from users who are not on its list. A call that supplies the journal's id was not refused in testing."
      }
    ],
