    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Do I need the free app as well?",
        "a": "Yes. Lost Messages Routing is free and does the capturing; Lost Message Recovery adds the routing, the rules, the groups and the audit log on top of what it stores."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does it change how Odoo handles mail?",
        "a": "No. Odoo still bounces, rejects and ignores mail as before. The free app only notes why, and a reply to a deleted record is recorded while Odoo still creates its own new record."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can it recover every lost mail?",
        "a": "No. A mail that was never captured, or whose stored source was purged, cannot be replayed, and the app says so."
      },
      {
        "q": "Could routing create two records?",
        "a": "Not from the same message. A message that is already Recovered is refused, and a failed attempt creates nothing."
      },
      {
        "q": "Who can see the stored mail?",
        "a": "Managers. Reviewers see the sender, recipient and subject, but not the stored raw mail."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the stored email personal data?",
        "a": "Yes: it is the whole email. The stored source is blanked after 30 days by default, and you can change the period or keep it forever in Settings. Decide the period with your data protection lead; the app makes no compliance claim."
      },
      {
        "q": "What about mail that is not UTF-8?",
        "a": "The stored copy of such a mail is altered (section 8). It is a known defect and is not fixed in this version."
      }
    ],
